# A SEVEN-NODE SPLINE, constrained as far as a spline can be.
#
# Drawn loose on purpose -- none of these numbers is round -- so every
# constraint below has to MOVE something.

sketch Blade7

tool spline
click 8 -14
click 35 32
click 62 -6
click 90 26
click 118 -4
click 146 24
click 172 -12
finish

# The straight chord that closes the profile, drawn clear of the spline.
tool line
click 178 -30
click 2 -30

# The chord, pinned outright: 2 + 1 + 1 for its four freedoms.
constrain fix Line1.end
constrain horizontal Line1
dimension length Line1 180 as ChordLength

# ...and the spline's TWO ENDS pulled onto it.
constrain coincident Spline1.start Line1.end
constrain coincident Spline1.end Line1.start

pad Blade 6 as BladeThickness
solve
